{#
  module/SionModel/view/sion-model/sion-model/phpinfo.phtml, ported — a file whose
  entire content is `echo phpinfo();`.

  `|raw` is load-bearing and is the only thing this template does. phpinfo() emits
  HTML, generated by PHP itself from its own configuration, and autoescaping it would
  render a page of visible tags. It is not user input: every value in it comes from
  the ini and the loaded extensions.

  What arrives is a *complete* HTML document — doctype, <html>, <head>, <body> — so
  extending the layout nests one document inside another. The laminas rendering does
  exactly that (two doctypes, two <html>, two <body>, measured), and reproducing it is
  the point; see App\Controller\PhpInfoController for why it is not being fixed here.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
{{ php_info|raw }}
{% endblock %}
